UPDATE companies SET description='Topsy Products operates from Oshkosh, Wisconsin, as a custom design and fabrication shop specializing in automotive accessories. The company focuses on developing engineered solutions for off-road vehicles, though its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company designs and manufactures a range of hard-top removal systems and accessories for Jeep Wrangler models (JL, JK, TJ/YJ) and the Gladiator, as well as parts for the Ford Bronco. Its product line includes hinge hoist brackets and kits, hoist systems, door storage solutions, radio communications accessories, and general accessories. Each accessory undergoes in-house design engineering and development before fabrication.

Topsy Products serves the automotive aftermarket, targeting off-road enthusiasts and owners of Jeep and Ford Bronco vehicles.

The company emphasizes innovation, creative thinking, and attention to detail as core differentiators, stating that every accessory requires in-depth design engineering to meet specifications on budget and on time. This innovation-driven approach is cited as the foundation of its product development process.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom design engineering", "Fabrication", "Product development"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Off-road vehicle accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-depth design engineering and development for every accessory", "Creative thinking and attention to detail in product design", "Commitment to on-budget and on-time delivery", "Innovation-driven approach to each project"], "facts_used": ["Company name and headquarters (Oshkosh, Wisconsin) -> db", "Description as custom design and fabricator -> /", "Product categories: Jeep Wrangler (JL, JK, TJ/YJ, Gladiator) and Ford Bronco accessories -> /", "Emphasis on design engineering, innovation, on-budget/on-time delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Topy Products is an innovative custom design and fabricator.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='topsy-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Toray Plastics (America), Inc. operates its headquarters in North Kingstown, Rhode Island, where its Torayfan® and Lumirror® film divisions are based. A second facility in Front Royal, Virginia houses the PEF foam division. The company is a wholly owned subsidiary of Toray Industries, Inc., a Japanese multinational founded in 1926 with over 47,900 employees across 308 subsidiaries worldwide. No founding date for the U.S. entity is disclosed, and the original founders are not named in public materials.

The company manufactures specialty polymer films and foams for converters and manufacturers that produce finished consumer and industrial goods. The Torayfan® division extrudes polypropylene and cast polypropylene films, including metallized OPP and bio-based PET variants. The Lumirror® division produces polyester (PET) films, also offered in metallized and bio-based grades. The PEF division extrudes polyolefin, polypropylene, and polyethylene foams. Together the divisions run multiple extrusion, metallizing, and coating lines, including proprietary LumiLid® extrusion coating systems (XXL5 and TXL5). Facility sizes and annual volumes are not published.

Toray''s films and foams serve packaging, label, solar-control window, technical, housing and engineering, and automotive markets. Converters use the materials for food packaging that extends shelf life, for pressure-sensitive labels, for automotive window tinting, and for solar-control glazing in buildings and vehicles. The company cites automotive window tinting and food packaging as specific application examples.

Toray states its corporate philosophy is to contribute to society through the creation of new value with innovative ideas, technologies, and products. The U.S. operation emphasizes environmental sustainability, holding certifications such as ISO 14001, ISCC PLUS, and Rhode Island Green Manufacturing Certification, and frames its manufacturing approach as responsible stewardship for future generations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','BRC (GFSI)','Sedex','IMS (FDA Milk Packaging)','ISCC PLUS (VA)','ISCC PLUS (RI)','Rhode Island Green Manufacturing Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polypropylene film extrusion", "Cast polypropylene film extrusion", "Polyester (PET) film extrusion", "Metallizing (OPP, PET)", "Bio-based PET film production", "Polyolefin foam extrusion", "Polypropylene foam extrusion", "Polyethylene foam extrusion", "Hot stamping / Cold foil", "Casting sheet for PPF", "Extrusion coating", "LumiLid\u00ae extrusion coating (XXL5, TXL5)"], "industries": ["Packaging", "Labels", "Solar Control Window Films", "Technical Films", "Housing & Engineering", "Automotive", "Automotive Window Tinting"], "materials": ["Polypropylene", "Cast Polypropylene", "Polyester (PET)", "Metallized OPP", "Metallized PET", "Bio-based PET", "Polyolefin", "Polypropylene Foam", "Polyethylene Foam"], "equipment": ["LumiLid\u00ae extrusion coating lines (XXL5, TXL5)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["State-of-the-art equipment at both U.S. facilities", "Global leadership in polypropylene, polyester, and polyolefin foam markets", "Comprehensive sustainability certifications including ISO 14001, ISCC PLUS, and Rhode Island Green Manufacturing Certification", "Integrated film and foam divisions under one corporate structure", "Proprietary LumiLid\u00ae extrusion coating technology for large-format applications"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in North Kingstown, Rhode Island -> /about-us", "PEF Foam Division in Front Royal, Virginia -> /about-us", "Parent company Toray Industries founded 1926 -> /about-us", "Parent company 47,900 employees -> /about-us", "Torayfan\u00ae Division manufactures polypropylene and cast polypropylene films -> /", "Lumirror\u00ae Division manufactures polyester film -> /", "PEF Division produces polyolefin, polypropylene, and polyethylene foams -> /", "Metallized OPP and PET and bio-based PET films available -> /", "Industries served: packaging, labels, solar control window, technical, housing & engineering, automotive -> /", "Automotive window tinting application -> /industries_served", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 14001, BRC, Sedex, IMS, ISCC PLUS (VA), ISCC PLUS (RI), Rhode Island Green Manufacturing Certification -> /about-us", "Sustainability commitment -> /about-us", "Capabilities: Hot Stamping/Cold Foil, Casting Sheet for PPF, Extrusion Coated, LumiLid\u00ae Extrusion Coated XXL5, LumiLid\u00ae Extrusion Coated TXL5 -> db", "Headquarters city/state from database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our Torayfan\u00ae Division manufactures polypropylene and cast polypropylene films. The Lumirror\u00ae Division manufactures polyester film. ... Toray''s PEF Division produces polyolefin, polypropylene, and polyethylene foams.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='toray-plastics-america-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Torque King 4x4 operates from Billings, Montana. The company, formerly known as QUAD 4x4, does not disclose its founding year or original founders. It is led by Vice President Dan Guarino, who has represented the firm in national media discussions about domestic manufacturing.

The business functions as a manufacturer, a stocking distributor of OEM components, and an exporter. Its product range covers 4x4 special tools, genuine original-equipment parts, aftermarket parts, and service kits for vehicles dating from 1941 to current models. The catalog includes power-train components under the Torque King brand, as well as parts for Dana-Spicer axles, Ford Sterling axles, AAM axles, New Process/New Venture transfer cases, NV4500 and NV5600 transmissions, Getrag G360 transmissions, BorgWarner T19 transmissions, and related driveshafts. The company also produces color-illustrated shop manuals and technical service bulletins.

Customers include individual truck owners and fleet managers across work, hauling, towing, and recreational use. The supported brands span Dodge, Ram, GMC, Chevrolet, Ford, Jeep, International, and Mahindra Roxor. The company emphasizes expert guidance to help clients select correct parts for axle, hub, transmission, and transfer-case repairs.

Torque King positions itself around U.S.-based manufacturing and supply-chain reshoring. In a televised segment on Viewpoint with Dennis Quaid, Guarino highlighted the importance of domestic production for economic resilience. The firm promotes its Montana base, deep technical library, and video-based repair guides as differentiators that keep trucks on the road.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["4x4 power train component manufacturing", "OEM parts distribution", "Exporting", "Technical manual and service bulletin publishing", "Video-based technical guides", "Expert parts consultation", "Mahindra Roxor front hub service guidance"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Commercial fleet maintenance", "Off-road vehicle parts", "Heavy-duty truck parts"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Montana-based manufacturer and OEM parts distributor with export capabilities", "Publishes proprietary shop manuals and technical service bulletins for 4x4 vehicles", "Covers vehicle platforms from 1941 to present, including hard-to-find small parts", "Provides expert technical guidance and video repair tutorials (Torque King TV)", "Advocates for U.S. manufacturing reshoring, featured on Viewpoint with Dennis Quaid"], "facts_used": ["Location: Billings, Montana -> db", "Formerly QUAD 4x4 -> /about-us", "Business description: manufacturer, stocking OEM parts distributor, exporter -> /about-us", "Product range: 4x4 special tools, genuine OEM parts, aftermarket parts, service kits, shop manuals, technical service bulletins -> /about-us", "Vehicle coverage: 1941 to present, brands Dodge, Ram, GMC, Chevrolet, Ford, Jeep, International, Mahindra Roxor -> / and /about-us", "Specific components: Dana-Spicer axles, Ford Sterling axles, AAM axles, New Process/New Venture transfer cases, NV4500/NV5600 transmissions, Getrag G360, BorgWarner T19, driveshafts -> /about-us", "Vice President: Dan Guarino -> 