UPDATE companies SET description='The company was founded in 1993 by Daniel Gugnoni, a sculptor who turned to furniture making after earning a BFA. He established the business on the Shaker principles of hard work, honesty, and pride in craftsmanship. Barbara Mojon Gugnoni, who holds a BA in English literature and a background in advertising, joined the operation in 1996 and now handles marketing, sales, and the finishing process.

The studio produces one-of-a-kind and custom fine art furniture, each piece designed and built by Daniel Gugnoni. The workflow moves from client consultation through design, handcrafted joinery, and a proprietary twelve-step hand-rubbed finish applied by Barbara. The shop does not run production lines; every item is a unique functional sculpture. The facility is a small country barn studio and a second-floor gallery where finished pieces are displayed.

Troy Brook Visions has exhibited at juried events such as the American Craft Council Shows, the Paradise City Arts Festival, the Philadelphia Invitational Furniture Show, and the Fine Furnishings Show. These venues connect the studio with buyers who value handcrafted, design-driven furniture for residential settings.

The founders say the business exists to honor the material and the maker. Daniel Gugnoni describes each board as a gift from nature that should not be squandered, and the couple emphasizes that they never manufacture product—they create art. The Shaker-inspired ethos and the direct, personal involvement of both artisans in every commission are presented as the core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Fine art furniture fabrication", "Twelve-step hand-rubbed finishing", "Sculpture-inspired design", "Client consultation and design collaboration"], "industries": ["Fine art furniture", "Custom furniture", "High-end residential furnishings", "Interior design", "Artisan craft"], "materials": ["Wood (various species)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Shaker philosophy of hard work, honesty, and pride in craftsmanship", "One-of-a-kind custom pieces designed and built by the founders", "Twelve-step hand-rubbed finishing process", "Participation in prestigious juried craft shows (American Craft Council, Paradise City Arts Festival, etc.)", "Direct client collaboration from design through delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1993 by Daniel Gugnoni -> /about-us", "Located in Litchfield, Connecticut -> /", "Barbara Mojon Gugnoni joined in 1996 -> /about-us", "Creates custom handcrafted fine art furniture -> /", "Uses twelve-step finishing process -> /about-us", "Participates in American Craft Council Shows, Paradise City Arts Festival, Philadelphia Invitational Furniture Show, Fine Furnishings Show -> /about-us", "Operates studio and gallery in a red barn -> /", "Shaker philosophy of hard work, honesty, and pride in craftsmanship -> /about-us", "One-of-a-kind pieces, no manufacturing -> /", "Direct client collaboration -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Master Artisan Daniel Gugnoni designs and creates exquisite custom handcrafted fine art furniture.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='troy-brook-visions-fine-art-furniture-gallery-and-studio' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='True Position Plastics, LLC is based in Duncan, Oklahoma. The company was founded by Justin Church, a tooling and mold design expert with over 25 years of hands-on experience in the plastics industry. Church began his career as a machinist and mold maker, spending more than a decade as a mold designer before advancing to Tooling Manager and Tooling Engineer roles, complex programs from concept through production.

The firm provides plastic injection molding services sourced through both domestic and overseas tooling partners, managing the full process from mold construction to production parts. Its core capabilities include scientific molding, liquid silicone rubber (LSR) molding, insert molding, and overmolding. In addition, True Position Plastics offers complete mold design services for prototype and production molds (SPI Class 101–105), mold flow analysis, SimForm cooling analysis, CNC machining, and design-for-manufacturability reviews focused on gating, venting, cooling, and ejection. No facility size, headcount, or volume figures are disclosed.

The company serves the medical, consumer, automotive, industrial, and telecommunications sectors. Customers range from medical device manufacturers needing validated components to consumer product developers and automotive suppliers requiring production-grade tooling and molded parts.

